  <prompt>Author `.claude/adr/ADR-050-canonical-modal-shell.md` — a CONCISE ADR (Decision + MUST / MUST NOT constraints + brief rationale) for the canonical modal shell, referencing ADR-021 and ADR-023. The owner chose a NEW focused ADR over extending ADR-021 (spec Decisions §11-C: greppable, self-contained). Then add an index row to `.claude/adr/INDEX.md`. This is FR-10 and MUST run in the main session (the write boundary in CLAUDE.md §3 blocks sub-agents from `.claude/`). Documentation only — no code.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Fluent UI v9, ADR authoring, and Spaarke architecture governance. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>`.claude/adr/ADR-050-canonical-modal-shell.md` exists as a concise ADR with explicit MUST / MUST NOT constraints and references to ADR-021 + ADR-023; `.claude/adr/INDEX.md` carries a new ADR-050 row with title + key constraint + status.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Design §7 deliverable #4 / spec Decisions §11-C: the owner resolved "extend ADR-021 vs new focused ADR" in favor of a NEW concise ADR titled "Canonical Modal Shell" that references ADR-021/023 so the decision is greppable and self-contained. The project strengthens ADR-021 (bans `'1px'`/inline colors in modals) and preserves ADR-023 (`ChoiceModal` re-base) — there are no ADR tensions to resolve, only constraints to codify. The next-free ADR number is ADR-050 (ADR-049 is the current highest — verified in `.claude/adr/INDEX.md`).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">.claude/adr/ADR-050-canonical-modal-shell.md</file>
      <file role="modify">.claude/adr/INDEX.md</file>
      <file role="reference">.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file role="reference">.claude/adr/ADR-023-choice-dialog-pattern.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarke-modal-system/spec.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="004" status="pending">The `SprkModal` base shell whose composition + constraints this ADR codifies.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">ADR MUST rules to codify: compose `RecordNavigationModalShell` + `ModalWindowControls` (do not fork or parallel-abstract them); keep the Fluent `Dialog`/`DialogSurface` envelope (transform-robust portal); realize `--sprk-ui-scale` via a scaled Fluent theme (multiply px tokens); use semantic tokens only (no hex, no `'1px'` literals, no inline color styles); scroll the body natively with a thin scrollbar.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">ADR MUST NOT rules to codify: hand-rolled `position:fixed`/`createElement` overlays; CSS `zoom` for scaling; per-surface bespoke chrome (each surface's modal is a thin config of `SprkModal`, never a new envelope).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">The ADR references ADR-021 (Fluent v9, semantic tokens) as the parent it strengthens — state the strengthening (bans `'1px'` + inline color in modal components) rather than restating ADR-021 in full.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-023">The ADR references ADR-023 (Choice Dialog Pattern) as preserved via the `ChoiceModal` re-base — do NOT supersede or contradict it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Use ADR-050 (next-free number — ADR-049 is highest). Match the concise-ADR house style in `.claude/adr/` (Decision / Constraints / Key patterns / Rationale, ~100-150 lines). Add exactly one INDEX.md row. NEW ADR + INDEX edit are both under `.claude/` — main session only (§3).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Canonical modal shell ADR</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-modal-system/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-modal-system/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-modal-system/design.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/INDEX.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-023-choice-dialog-pattern.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="record-modal-selection" location=".claude/patterns/ui/record-modal-selection.md">The modal decision layer this ADR sits beneath.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load spec Decisions §11-C, design §10, ADR-021, ADR-023, and confirm in `.claude/adr/INDEX.md` that ADR-050 is the next-free number. Declare RIGOR: STANDARD.</step>
    <step order="1">Author `.claude/adr/ADR-050-canonical-modal-shell.md` in the concise-ADR house style: Title "Canonical Modal Shell", Status, Decision (one canonical `SprkModal` shell + thin presets, composing existing primitives).</step>
    <step order="2">Write the MUST constraints (compose primitives; Fluent `Dialog` envelope; scaled-theme `--sprk-ui-scale`; semantic tokens only; native thin scrollbar).</step>
    <step order="3">Write the MUST NOT constraints (hand-rolled overlays; CSS zoom; per-surface bespoke chrome) and a References section citing ADR-021 (strengthened) + ADR-023 (preserved) + ADR-012.</step>
    <step order="4">Add a brief Rationale (1-2 sentences) tying to the design's "compose, don't create" principle and the 4K scaled-theme decision.</step>
    <step order="5">Add one ADR-050 row to `.claude/adr/INDEX.md` (ADR | Title | Key Constraint | Status).</step>
    <step order="6">Re-read both files for house-style + reference accuracy; confirm ADR-050 does not collide with an existing number.</step>
    <step order="7">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set 011 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document any deviation in `projects/spaarke-modal-system/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="adr-aware">Load applicable ADRs for house-style + reference accuracy</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">.claude/adr/ADR-050-canonical-modal-shell.md</output>
    <output type="doc">.claude/adr/INDEX.md</output>
